  "limits": [
    "Prepared owning references remain available until actual callee entry. The source holding identity is retained; another owner of the same region cannot replace that selected handle. Duplicate, early and repeated consumption are checked statically.",
    "Cleanup paths carry unreachable guarantees, owning-handle availability and region liveness. Original-completion selection protects materialized return holders without reviving consumed names. Discarded/replaced/abandoned results release under the same retained-owner rule as scope cleanup.",
    "The native harness injects one failed owning registration; its catch consumes the still-owned source. A10000-iteration explicit-scope phase acquires/transfers/releases10000 regions with one record live at peak. Native resource counters assert exact release. Generated LLVM and runtime C++ are ASAN-instrumented.",
    "The prior64-acquisition observation was0.351s. Preliminary broader analysis measured32.64s with per-query closure,5.71s with all-node batching and1.28s with demanded-root batching. Final measurements are listed separately. This change adds analysis cost; these single observations do not establish a general complexity or speed guarantee.",
    "No native ownership/record layout, allocator, relocation, RTTI, owner-union or source-policy change. D16 fractions, D22 pending construction choices and pure/TCO/compiler-pilot deferral remain.",
    "Full callable/AOT/defer goal remains incomplete. Non-queryable provenance, broader relational owner/target/result proofs, remaining owning-call composition, generic capture transport, process-lifetime module queues and family/AOT integration remain work."
  ]
